Subject: Galt's Island ? 

Before you Galt fans go and buy a piece of Russian tundra here's one
piece of information you might find interesting.  It was on Finnish
TV a while ago.

  In the South East Pacific is a small little known British colony
called Pitcairn Islands.  There are four islands, only one of which is
inhabited.  The inhabitants are planning to apply for independence
from Britain in the future.  They will have three "extra" islands -
maybe they could sell one or two to raise funds for their tiny
government. I recall there are only about 100 inhabitants, which is
why the U.K. might be reluctant to grant the Pitcairn Islanders
independence.  What makes this case so special is that such a small
nation could really grant the purchaser of an island sovereignity -
legal sovereignity according to international law.  I doubt Russia
(or most other countries) would ever do that.  Even the remotest areas
usually have at least some inhabitants.

   Surely this is a chance worth studying.  Do keep us up-to-date how
your interestng Libertaria-project is doing.

